      "explain": "A <strong>structure</strong> is a user-defined data type that groups variables of <strong>different types</strong> under a single name. Each variable inside is called a <strong>member</strong>. You access a member using the <strong>membership (dot) operator</strong> <code>.</code>, as in <code>s1.roll</code>. Structures can hold arrays, can be nested inside other structures, and you can make an array of structures to store many records.",
