      "examAnswer": "A structure is a user-defined data type that groups together variables of different data types under a single name, where each variable is called a member. It is declared using the struct keyword, and the declaration serves only as a template; memory is allocated when a structure variable is created. Members are accessed using the membership or dot operator, for example s1.roll. A structure may contain arrays as members, may be nested within another structure, and an array of structures may be declared to store multiple records. The size of a structure is at least the sum of the sizes of its members and may be larger due to padding inserted by the compiler for alignment.",
      "remember": "struct = one form holding many different fields. Dot for a variable, index-then-dot for an array of them.",
