      "explain": "A <strong>union</strong> looks like a structure but all its members <strong>share the same memory space</strong>, so its size equals the size of its <strong>largest member</strong> and only one member holds a valid value at any moment. An <strong>enum</strong> creates a named list of integer constants, making code readable. <strong>typedef</strong> gives an existing type a new, shorter name.",
